omes plan after affordable housing offer falls from 40% to 12%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135617920.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Southwark Council's planning committee voted unanimously against Berkeley Homes' revised plans for the Bermondsey Place development. The housebuilder proposed reducing affordable housing from 40 percent to just 12 percent, causing strong local opposition. Council members expressed concerns about the long timeline for home completion and questioned the developer's financial figures. Berkeley Homes highlighted rising costs and council fees as reasons for the reduced affordable housing offer.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/berkeley-homes-proposed-1060-homes-in-later-phases-of-a-london-scheme-and-cut-the-developments-overall-affordable-housing-commitment-from-40-to-12-councillors-unanimously-rejected-the-revision/articleshow/135617920.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/berkeley-homes-proposed-1060-homes-in-later-phases-of-a-london-scheme-and-cut-the-developments-overall-affordable-housing-commitment-from-40-to-12-councillors-unanimously-rejected-the-revision/articleshow/135617920.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T23:57:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135618156,imgsize-119281.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Court upholds sale of divorced Arkansas woman's property share after her bankruptcy filing.]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135615724.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a landmark ruling, a federal appeals court upheld the sale of a divorced woman's stake in property located in Arkansas. The decision favored her bankruptcy trustee, overcoming objections posed by her ex-husband. He contended that the buyer's good faith was not adequately proven in prior hearings but failed to voice this concern earlier. Consequently, the property transaction with Blue Sun Capital LLC is deemed legally binding.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arkansas-couple-bought-property-together-in-2021-and-divorced-less-than-a-year-later-each-keeping-half-after-the-woman-remarried-and-filed-for-bankruptcy-a-court-dismissed-his-challenge-to-the-sale-of-her-share/articleshow/135615724.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arkansas-couple-bought-property-together-in-2021-and-divorced-less-than-a-year-later-each-keeping-half-after-the-woman-remarried-and-filed-for-bankruptcy-a-court-dismissed-his-challenge-to-the-sale-of-her-share/articleshow/135615724.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T23:46:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135617866,imgsize-208991.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Cristiano Ronaldo turned a Madeira nightclub into an $8 million home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135605640.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2018-cristiano-ronaldo-bought-lisbons-record-breaking-7-million-apartment-before-turning-a-former-madeira-nightclub-into-an-8-million-seven-storey-home-in-2019/articleshow/135605640.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2018-cristiano-ronaldo-bought-lisbons-record-breaking-7-million-apartment-before-turning-a-former-madeira-nightclub-into-an-8-million-seven-storey-home-in-2019/articleshow/135605640.cms]]></guid>